{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-unstable-atom","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:unstable-atom","kind":"definition","title":"Unstable atom (failure of normal-form positivity)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-stable-atom"],"tags":["instability","decay","ilp","atom","phase-boundary"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.UnstableAtom","text":"unstable-atom.md","leanSource":"unstable-atom.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:unstable-atom\"></a><p><em>An atom-knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> is <strong>unstable at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code></strong> if and only if it fails to satisfy the <a href=\"#def:stable-atom\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/atom-isotope-knots\">stable atom</a> condition. That is, the coefficient vector <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x(K, q)</code> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_w</code> within the confinement filtration <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J^{\\ell(K, q)}(q)</code> either fails to lie in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}_{\\geq 0}^N</code> or violates <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{G}(q)\\,x(K, q) \\geq 0</code> in some coordinate.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/unstable-atom.md","heading":"Definition","number":"9.10.12","page":"b/def-unstable-atom","qa":{"counts":{"pass":79,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":65},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BraidKnot.UnstableAtom","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/unstable-atom.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
